window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"ryze","b":"locke","win":["Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Ryze"],"spikes":[{"when":"Level 2","text":"The whole trade game starts hinging on whether your W root lands — make it count."},{"when":"Levels 4-5","text":"Hold Rune Prison for his dash — the auto wind-up after it is the tell."},{"when":"Mana items online","text":"Your item-bound power finally arrives — the even lane starts leaning your way."},{"when":"Two-plus items","text":"Mana-stacked Overload spam out-scales and out-DPSes him — the endgame is yours here."}],"wants":{"you":["W root saved for his E dash commit","Even farming into your item spikes","Extended fights where Q spam compounds"],"foe":["Rune Prison spent before Flux lands","You chunked into Purgatory execute range","The game decided before your items"]},"early":"The entire laning phase is even, and that is fine — even is winning for a scaler. His on-hit walk-ups answer your poke, so the lane hinges on the root: with Spell Flux on him Rune Prison roots, without it the cage only slows, so hold it for his dash — a flat 10 seconds — rather than spending it on cooldown.","mid":"Six changes little — Realm Warp is macro power, not a dueling tool — and even his first item does not break the stalemate. Keep your HP respectable so Purgatory never has an execute window, shove and warp for map plays, and buy every mana item on schedule; your inflection point is coming.","late":"Two-plus items and the matchup finally breaks open: mana-stacked Overload spam out-scales and out-DPSes him outright. Fight extended windows where Spell Flux into Rune Prison recycles every few seconds, save the root for his 10-second dash, and stay above execute range from here.","whys":["Level 1 is even — your Q poke is answered by his on-hit walk-ups, so neither side leads.","At 2 trades stay skill-based, gated almost entirely on whether your W root lands.","Level 3 stays even: Rune Prison can't be dodged, but with no Flux it only slows.","Levels 4-5 revolve around who wins the root mind-game — a pure skill stage.","At 6 it is still even: your power is item-bound and has not arrived yet.","First item keeps it even — Realm Warp is macro, not a dueling tool, and neither of you has a decisive edge.","Post-items your mana-stacked Overload spam out-scales and out-DPSes him — the late game is yours."]});
