window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"ryze","b":"zaahen","win":["Skill","Zaahen","Zaahen","Zaahen","Skill","Zaahen","Zaahen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Zaahen level 2","text":"His trade tools come online against a squishy, immobile target — the bleeding starts here."},{"when":"Zaahen level 3","text":"Aureate Rush walks you down and his Glaive recast knocks you up; give up trades, keep the farm."},{"when":"Your level 6","text":"Realm Warp does not duel, but a pre-placed warp voids his entire all-in — your survival tool."},{"when":"Zaahen first item","text":"Grievous Wounds is the buy that helps — his Q and R both heal. Play the map, not the lane."}],"wants":{"you":["Max farm with minimum exposure","A warp or root answer ready for his engage","Teamfights where range replaces dueling"],"foe":["An immobile target he can walk down","Duels forced anywhere on the map","Your escape tools burned before he commits"]},"early":"Level 1 is even, then the lane turns hostile: from 2 he out-threatens a squishy, immobile Ryze, and by 3 his Q and E walk you down straight through Rune Prison. Concede the trades, not the farm — take what the wave allows, hug your side, and demand jungle attention early rather than after first blood.","mid":"At 6 the stage evens out on a technicality worth mastering: his R is the kill button and yours is not, but a pre-placed Realm Warp or a clean root as he commits voids the entire all-in. After his first item the gap widens beyond what defensive buys can close, so shove-and-warp for map value instead.","late":"Late he deletes you in any duel you cannot avoid — so avoid all of them. Move with your team, warp the squad for picks and objectives he cannot answer alone, and fight from maximum range behind CC. Your scaling shows up in teamfights; his shows up in the 1v1 you must never grant him.","whys":["Level 1 is an even skill lane — his trade tools are not online yet.","At 2 he already out-threatens a squishy, immobile Ryze in any real trade.","By 3 Aureate Rush closes the gap and slices for percent health.","Levels 4-5 stay his: you have no mobility to escape once he commits the engage.","At 6 his R kills and yours roams, but a pre-placed warp or clean root voids his all-in — the stage rides on your escape play.","His item widens a gap armour cannot close — Grievous Wounds is the stat that helps.","Late he gap-closes and deletes you, and a filled passive revives him — only the map answers him."]});
