window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"ryze","b":"masteryi","win":["Ryze","Ryze","Skill","Master Yi","Master Yi","Master Yi","Ryze"],"spikes":[{"when":"Level 1","text":"Overload poke backed by the Rune Prison threat beats him before his kit exists."},{"when":"Yi levels 4-5","text":"He all-ins the moment your root is down — track your own cooldown like a hawk."},{"when":"Yi first item","text":"Alpha Strike goes untargetable through your combo and out-DPSes you 1v1 alone."},{"when":"Two-plus items","text":"Your Flux rotation and the root swing teamfights decisively back your way."}],"wants":{"you":["Early chunks banked while he is weak","The root held until he commits","Grouped fights where your burst deletes him"],"foe":["Your Rune Prison baited or down","Sidelane duels from first item on","Alpha Strike dodging your key spells"]},"early":"You bully the first two levels: Overload poke and the Rune Prison threat beat his empty early kit, and Spell Flux into the cage keeps him off the wave. Meditate is a channel on 10 seconds and your W cancels it outright — never let him heal the poke back. At 3 his kit evens it, and through 4-5 he all-ins the second your root lapses.","mid":"From 6 the pressure is his: Realm Warp is utility while Highlander, 85 seconds, duels — and it makes him immune to slows, so a cage without Spell Flux on him does nothing. His first item lets him out-DPS you alone. Do not sidelane against him; shove, warp to your team, and cash his splitpush for objectives elsewhere.","late":"Two-plus items swings it back: cycling Flux rotations and Rune Prison are exactly what a reset-reliant Yi hates. Highlander shrugs the slow, so land Spell Flux first. Group every fight, root the instant he commits, and delete him inside it. He beats Ryze the duelist; he loses to Ryze the teamfight machine.","whys":["Your Overload poke and Rune Prison root threat beat him at level 1.","Your W root into the E combo keeps him off you entirely at 2.","At 3 Alpha Strike arrives — untargetable on a 20-second cooldown, so burst spent into it is wasted and trades even out.","Through 4-5 he all-ins whenever your W root is down and wins — his stage.","At 6 your Realm Warp is utility while his Highlander duels — the kill pressure stays his.","With his first item he Alpha Strikes through your combo and out-DPSes you 1v1.","Late your Flux rotations and Rune Prison swing teamfights back to you — you out-scale where it matters."]});
